# Analysing Bank of England Decisions and UK Bank Stocks

I've been interested in programming for quite a long time. My dad first introduced me to Python when I was younger, and I continued developing my understanding of it through GCSE Computer Science. Since then, I've used programming in various projects, although until recently, very little of that had involved financial data.

Now that I'm studying Economics and Finance at university, I wanted to find a way to combine the two. In particular, I was interested in taking something I had learnt about in economics, such as monetary policy, and examining how it actually relates to financial markets.

This led me to a question: **how do UK bank shares behave around Bank of England interest rate decisions, and does that behaviour differ depending on whether rates are raised, cut or held?**

It seemed like a relatively straightforward question at first. As I worked through the project, I realised there was considerably more to it than downloading some share prices and comparing them.

